# Operator UI credibility (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08): **UI quality is a credibility
issue and high priority.** Operators and auditors judge AIC on fonts,
spacing, judicious color and icons, and whether interfaces look and
work professionally. Poor layouts, clipping, overlaps, non-working
controls, crashes, hangs, and weak menu/dialog design **cost
credibility**. Treat these as **high-priority defects**, not polish
backlog.

## The rule

> **Operators and auditors judge AIC on fonts, spacing, judicious
> color and icons, and whether interfaces look and work
> professionally. Poor layouts, clipping, overlaps, non-working
> controls, crashes, hangs, and weak menu/dialog design cost
> credibility. Treat these as high-priority defects, not polish
> backlog.**

Applies to **every** operator GUI in the workspace: Win32 dialogs,
Tauri shells, product launchers, elevate helpers, and the admin SPA
where visual/behavioral quality is customer-visible.

## Concrete requirements — agents MUST

1. **Priority** — When both are in scope, fix UI credibility defects
   before optional feature chrome. Credibility defects are **P0**.
2. **Fonts** — Readable professional sizes; no micro-type; consistent
   type hierarchy (headers vs body vs captions). Match sibling AIC
   dialogs in the same binary / design system.
3. **Spacing / margins** — Obey
   [`gui-margins-and-spacing.mdc`](gui-margins-and-spacing.mdc): no
   dead top whitespace; headers close to their controls; consistent
   outer inset.
4. **Color** — Judicious use; accessible contrast (Section 508 /
   WCAG 2.0 AA); never convey meaning by color alone; no garish
   default AI purple-on-white / purple-to-indigo gradients on
   operator tools.
5. **Icons** — Real AIC brand assets from `core-assets` per
   [`branding-assets.mdc`](branding-assets.mdc). Never ship broken,
   missing, or placeholder icons on customer-facing dialogs.
6. **Layout** — No clipping; no overlaps; primary actions visible
   without horizontal scroll per
   [`essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc`](essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc).
7. **Behavior** — No crashes, hangs, or unresponsive UI. Controls
   must accept input and do what their labels say. Menus and dialogs
   must be coherent (clear titles, expected dismiss paths, no orphan
   or dead menu items).
8. **Acceptance** — A claim that a GUI element or feature is fixed,
   available, visible, or working requires screenshot or
   bounding-box proof the agent actually inspected (same bar as
   [`essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc`](essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc)).
9. **Read-only content** — Normal contrast; never fade important
   read-only values per
   [`readable-read-only-controls.mdc`](readable-read-only-controls.mdc).
10. **Windows shell output** — Do not emit ANSI / VT100 escape
    sequences into classic Windows Command Prompt or PowerShell
    panes per
    [`no-ansi-vt100-windows-shells.mdc`](no-ansi-vt100-windows-shells.mdc).

## Forbidden constructs

- Shipping a configurator / operator dialog with micro-type labels,
  uneven random gaps, or a large empty top dead zone.
- Broken image controls, missing `.ico` / header bitmaps, or
  generic placeholder icons on shipping surfaces.
- Primary actions clipped off-screen; overlapping rows/cells;
  controls that do not respond or that lie about their effect.
- Reporting a UI fix as done on build success alone, without a named
  screenshot or Playwright bounding-box artifact.
- Treating layout / typography / broken-control bugs as “polish
  later” when the same slice is already touching that surface.

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation** (configurator Settings dialog, conceptual):

```text
- 72 px empty spacer above the first field (dead top zone)
- Section title "Server connection" then 48 px gap before the URL edit
- 8 pt gray labels (micro-type); purple gradient banner chrome
- Header bitmap path points at a missing file → blank icon strip
- "Test connectivity" button painted past the right edge at 1024 px
- Clicking Save shows "ok" toast but the field handler is a no-op
```

An auditor opens the tool once and concludes the product is unfinished.
That is a **credibility** failure, not a backlog item.

**Fix** (same change set):

```text
- Outer inset ≥ 12–16 px; no empty hero spacer
- Title with ~8 px to first control; larger gap only between sections
- Body ≥ readable dialog font (match sibling AIC dialogs); clear H1/body
- Neutral professional chrome; WCAG AA contrast; status text not color-only
- Sync real `aic-header.png` / `.ico` from core-assets (branding-assets)
- Pin or fit so Test connectivity is visible at 1280 and 1024
- Wire Save to the real AppConfig write; prove with screenshot after deploy
```

